# Sport History Clue

You are building **Sport History Clue**, a daily sports-history guessing game in the spirit of Wordle, Framed, and Heardle.

Players are shown progressive archival clues — a tightly cropped image plate, redacted box-score stats, and period text — and must name the moment and the year. Extra clues, wrong event guesses, and year distance all deduct points. Scoring is authoritative on the server.

## Product rules

- Two modes: **Daily Brief** (one UTC puzzle for everyone) and **Expeditions** (time-travel campaigns through sports eras).
- A round has up to six clues. Clue 1 is free. Later clues cost points.
- Guess = event name (fuzzy aliases) + four-digit year.
- Never ship answers, aliases, or the true year to the client. The catalog is server-only (`src/lib/catalog.ts`).
- Validate every submitted score in `src/app/api` using `src/lib/scoring.ts` and `src/lib/normalize.ts`.
- Answer matching is **server-side only**: strip accents (NFD), case-insensitive, punctuation-folded. Do not trust the client.
- Historical facts must be accurate. Do not use disasters, deaths, or abuse as puzzle subjects.
- Autocomplete is a large event dictionary, not the day's answer list.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router (src/ directory) · TypeScript strict · Tailwind CSS v4
- shadcn-style primitives in `src/components/ui` (no Radix `asChild`)
- Framer Motion for clue-reveal transitions (`src/components/game/clues/`)
- Supabase (`src/lib/supabase`) is optional persistence for validated scores; the game must work from the local catalog when env vars are missing
- Zod for API payloads

## Hard constraints

- **Never** add geographical map libraries (no Leaflet, Mapbox, Cesium, or equivalents). Archive plates are SVG illustrations, not maps.
- UI stays **dark-mode**: ink backgrounds, gold/amber accents, crisp serif headlines + mono labels.

## Layout (do not flatten)

```
src/app/page.tsx                 landing + mode selector
src/app/daily/page.tsx           daily challenge
src/app/expeditions/[slug]/page.tsx
src/app/api/                     scoring validation and public puzzle payloads
src/components/game/ClueCard.tsx
src/components/game/clues/       modular reveal components + Framer Motion
src/components/game/InputBar.tsx
src/components/game/ScoreCard.tsx
src/lib/normalize.ts             accent-stripping answer match
src/lib/scoring.ts
src/lib/supabase/
```

## UI

- Visual language: dark archive / newsreel. Gold and amber on ink. No light page chrome.
- Clue reveals must be modular React components with Framer Motion (`ClueReveal`, `ImageClue`, `StatsClue`, `TextClue`, `QuoteClue`).
- ClueCard must support image zoom/pan and redacted stats that unmask as clues advance.
- InputBar: year stepper + fuzzy event autocomplete.
- ScoreCard: post-round modal with breakdown, share line, and next action.

## When changing scoring

Update `src/lib/scoring.ts` and `src/lib/scoring.test.ts` together. Keep the share-card copy in sync with the formula names.
